      "flags": {},
      "order": 8,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "OPTIONAL EXTRA LoRAs\n\nThe RAVEN adapter is already inside the MODEL that RAVEN Model Loader returns, at a fixed strength of 1.0. It is mandatory and is not a knob.\n\nTo stack further LoRAs, insert one or more stock 'LoraLoaderModelOnly' nodes on the MODEL wire, between RAVEN Model Loader and RAVEN Streaming Sampler:\n\n  RAVEN Model Loader -> LoraLoaderModelOnly -> (more) -> RAVEN Streaming Sampler\n\nThe loader returns a standard MODEL (a stock static ModelPatcher), which is exactly why this works. Nothing else in the graph changes."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [520, 680],
      "size": [420, 320],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 9,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "MODEL FILES AND LIMITS\n\nPut the files in the standard ComfyUI folders (nothing is downloaded automatically):\n  models/diffusion_models/minimax_h3_fl2va_bf16.safetensors   (full, non-pruned BF16)\n  models/loras/minimax_h3_raven_streaming_lora_4nfe_preview.safetensors  (mandatory)\n  models/text_encoders/qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_nvfp4_awq.safetensors\n  models/vae/minimax_h3_video_vae_fp16.safetensors   -> video_vae AND the H3 node's vae input\n  models/vae/minimax_h3_audio_vae_fp32.safetensors   -> audio_vae\n\nGeometry is set on 'MiniMax H3 Image to Video', not on the sampler:\n  width/height multiples of 32, width*height <= 1376*768\n  length = 17k+5 with k>=1, i.e. 22 minimum and 362 maximum; above 192 is experimental\n\nT2VA only: leave first_frame / last_frame unconnected. No CFG, no negative prompt, no sampler/scheduler choice. There is no per-chunk reroll: a chunk is committed to the KV cache as soon as it finishes.\n\nkv_cache_storage: leave it on 'cpu_pinned'. It keeps the KV cache in page-locked host RAM (~0.56 GiB on the card instead of ~21-28 GiB), which is what makes 1376x768 x 192 fit a 24 GiB VRAM envelope. 'gpu' is only for cards with room to spare. It changes where bytes live, not what is computed.\n\nRAM, not VRAM, is the usual limit: measured peak host RSS was ~129.9 GiB at 192 frames and ~135.0 GiB at 362. Budget 160 GiB available / 192 GB physical; 128 GiB will swap or OOM.\n\nSaving: SaveAnimatedWEBP + SaveAudio take IMAGE and AUDIO directly. For one muxed file, replace them with CreateVideo (fps 24) -> SaveVideo."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
